// Administrative Functions for SAM

+ shutdown{weight=10000}
* <id> eq <bot master> => Shutting down SAM system... ::::: shutdown -h now :::::
- {@botmaster only}

+ restart sam{weight=10000}
* <id> eq <bot master> => Restarting SAM services... ::::: systemctl restart sam :::::
- {@botmaster only}

+ reload config{weight=10000}
* <id> eq <bot master> => Reloading SAM configuration... ::::: kill -HUP `pgrep sam` :::::
- {@botmaster only}

+ debug mode on{weight=10000}
* <id> eq <bot master> => Enabling debug mode... ::::: debug all trace :::::
- {@botmaster only}

+ debug mode off{weight=10000}
* <id> eq <bot master> => Disabling debug mode... ::::: debug all error :::::
- {@botmaster only}

+ show logs{weight=10000}
* <id> eq <bot master> => Displaying SAM logs... ::::: tail -f /var/log/sam/sam.log :::::
- {@botmaster only}

+ clear logs{weight=10000}
* <id> eq <bot master> => Clearing SAM logs... ::::: echo > /var/log/sam/sam.log :::::
- {@botmaster only}

+ system stats{weight=10000}
* <id> eq <bot master> => Gathering system statistics... ::::: top -l 1 | head -20 :::::
- {@botmaster only}

+ memory usage{weight=10000}
* <id> eq <bot master> => Checking memory usage... ::::: ps aux --sort=-%mem | head -20 :::::
- {@botmaster only}

+ disk usage{weight=10000}
* <id> eq <bot master> => Checking disk usage... ::::: df -h :::::
- {@botmaster only}

+ network status{weight=10000}
* <id> eq <bot master> => Checking network status... ::::: netstat -rn :::::
- {@botmaster only}

+ service status{weight=10000}
* <id> eq <bot master> => Checking all service status... ::::: services :::::
- {@botmaster only}

+ update sam{weight=10000}
* <id> eq <bot master> => Updating SAM system... ::::: cd /opt/sam && git pull && cargo build --release :::::
- {@botmaster only}

+ backup config{weight=10000}
* <id> eq <bot master> => Backing up SAM configuration... ::::: cp -r /opt/sam/config /opt/sam/backup/config-`date +%Y%m%d` :::::
- {@botmaster only}

+ restore config{weight=10000}
* <id> eq <bot master> => This will restore configuration from backup. Are you sure? (Type 'confirm restore' to proceed)
- {@botmaster only}

+ confirm restore{weight=10000}
* <id> eq <bot master> => Restoring SAM configuration from latest backup... ::::: cp -r /opt/sam/backup/config-* /opt/sam/config :::::
- {@botmaster only}

+ emergency stop{weight=10000}
* <id> eq <bot master> => Emergency stop initiated... ::::: pkill -f sam :::::
- {@botmaster only}

+ reset sam{weight=10000}
* <id> eq <bot master> => This will reset SAM to default settings. Type 'confirm reset' to proceed.
- {@botmaster only}

+ confirm reset{weight=10000}
* <id> eq <bot master> => Resetting SAM to default configuration... ::::: cp /opt/sam/config/defaults/* /opt/sam/config/ :::::
- {@botmaster only}

+ botmaster only
- This command can only be used by my administrator. Access denied for user <id>.

+ set master *{weight=10000}
* <id> eq <bot master> => <set master=<star>>Master user updated to <star>.
- {@botmaster only}

+ add user *{weight=10000}
* <id> eq <bot master> => Adding user <star> to authorized users list...
- {@botmaster only}

+ remove user *{weight=10000}  
* <id> eq <bot master> => Removing user <star> from authorized users list...
- {@botmaster only}

+ list users{weight=10000}
* <id> eq <bot master> => Listing all authorized users...
- {@botmaster only}

+ change log level *{weight=10000}
* <id> eq <bot master> => Changing log level to <star>... ::::: debug all <star> :::::
- {@botmaster only}

+ enable service *{weight=10000}
* <id> eq <bot master> => Enabling service <star>... ::::: systemctl enable <star> :::::
- {@botmaster only}

+ disable service *{weight=10000}
* <id> eq <bot master> => Disabling service <star>... ::::: systemctl disable <star> :::::
- {@botmaster only}

+ maintenance mode on{weight=10000}
* <id> eq <bot master> => Entering maintenance mode...
- {@botmaster only}

+ maintenance mode off{weight=10000}
* <id> eq <bot master> => Exiting maintenance mode...
- {@botmaster only}

+ flush cache{weight=10000}
* <id> eq <bot master> => Flushing all caches... ::::: redis-cli flushall :::::
- {@botmaster only}

+ optimize database{weight=10000}
* <id> eq <bot master> => Optimizing SAM database... This may take a while...
- {@botmaster only}

+ vacuum database{weight=10000}
* <id> eq <bot master> => Running database vacuum... ::::: sqlite3 /opt/sam/data/sam.db "VACUUM;" :::::
- {@botmaster only}

+ health check{weight=10000}
* <id> eq <bot master> => Running comprehensive health check... ::::: /opt/sam/scripts/health_check.sh :::::
- {@botmaster only}

+ security scan{weight=10000}
* <id> eq <bot master> => Running security scan... This may take several minutes...
- {@botmaster only}

+ export data{weight=10000}
* <id> eq <bot master> => Exporting SAM data... ::::: /opt/sam/scripts/export_data.sh :::::
- {@botmaster only}

+ import data *{weight=10000}
* <id> eq <bot master> => Importing data from <star>... ::::: /opt/sam/scripts/import_data.sh <star> :::::
- {@botmaster only}

// General administrative info (available to all users)
+ admin help
- Administrative commands are available only to the system administrator.
- For basic help, try typing "help" to see available user commands.
- If you need administrative access, contact the system administrator.

+ who is the admin
- The current administrator is <bot master>.

+ sam version
- I'm SAM (Smart Assistant Manager) version <bot version>.
- You can also type "version" to get detailed version information.

+ system info
- I can provide system information. Type "status" for current system status.
- For detailed system info, try "system status" or "services".

// Error handling for unauthorized admin commands
+ * admin
- Administrative functions require special authorization.

+ sudo *
- I don't process sudo commands directly for security reasons. Administrative tasks should use the proper SAM admin commands.

+ su *  
- User switching is not available through SAM for security purposes.

> object shutdown python
    # Controlled shutdown
    import os
    os.system("echo 'SAM shutdown requested'")
    # Note: Actual shutdown should be handled by the system
< object
